{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. I've called us together because we have a time-sensitive situation. As you know, the company discovered unauthorized access to a customer-facing system, and the incident-response team has completed its initial review. Our board's regular meeting is tomorrow, and the company wants any required public filing approved before that meeting. Right now, there is no SEC Form 8-K drafted for this incident on our filing calendar. Under our normal pre-filing process, I need a final recommendation from each of you — cybersecurity, privacy, and investor relations — before I can authorize an external filing. I also want to flag that our board-approved communications process requires the final filing package to include a clear operational-continuity statement, omit ransom-demand details, and document board review before filing authorization. The existing draft communications use general language about an investigation but don't specify the incident's regulatory classification, affected-account count, detailed operational impact, or ransom-demand treatment. So before we go further, I need each of your recommendations: Do we need to file an 8-K for this incident, and if so, what should the filing package contain to meet our process requirements?"}
```

